{"availability":"available","full":"ChinmmayVShastrry/docchat-ai","name":"docchat-ai","description":"RAG-based document chat & summarization — hybrid BM25+semantic retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, multi-format docs, real-time streaming answers.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-22T17:47:21Z","updated":"2026-08-14T14:11:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://docchat-ai.streamlit.app","topics":["chromadb","gradio","llm","python","rag","streamlit"],"demo":"https://docchat-ai.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T19:52:39.685Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T19:52:39.685Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T19:52:39.685Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:35:03.912Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T19:49:12.033Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T19:52:39.685Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Retrieval-augmented document chat with source citations and a measured retrieval pipeline.","Upload PDFs, Word documents, spreadsheets or CSVs, get a structured summary, then ask questions answered only from the uploaded content — with inline citations, a visible view of the retrieved context, and a warning when the model strays beyond its sources.","Most RAG demos stop at \"embed, retrieve top-k, prompt\". That works on clean text and fails quietly everywhere else. This project is an attempt to build the parts that usually get skipped:"],"features":["Retrieval that combines two signals — keyword (BM25) and semantic (embeddings),","An evaluation harness that produces numbers, so retrieval changes can be justified","Ingestion that survives real documents — a fallback chain of four PDF parsers,","Honest failure modes — the system refuses when the answer isn't in the documents,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ChinmmayVShastrry/docchat-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"150e975ecf327eaeaa691d0e